body:
I can confirm the behavior and the reason I found is quite interesting.

The responsible for drawing the preview tile is a Control node in tile_map_layer_editor.cpp:997:
`p_overlay->draw_texture_rect_region(atlas_source->get_texture()...)`

This control node is created if non existing and assigned default values like texture filter In tile_map_layer_editor.cpp:3772
The filter value comes from edited_layer :
```
if (edited_layer && custom_overlay) {
	custom_overlay->set_texture_filter(edited_layer->get_texture_filter_in_tree());
}
```

edited_layer is a TileMapLayer, aka a CanvasItem. So get_texture_filter_in_tree() is:
```
CanvasItem::TextureFilter CanvasItem::get_texture_filter_in_tree() const {
	ERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(TEXTURE_FILTER_NEAREST);
	_refresh_texture_filter_cache();
	return (TextureFilter)texture_filter_cache;
}
```
and  its _refresh_texture_filter_cache():
```
void CanvasItem::_refresh_texture_filter_cache() const {
	if (!is_inside_tree()) {
		return;
	}

	if (texture_filter == TEXTURE_FILTER_PARENT_NODE) {
		CanvasItem *parent_item = get_parent_item();
		if (parent_item) {
			texture_filter_cache = parent_item->texture_filter_cache;
		} else {
			texture_filter_cache = RSE::CANVAS_ITEM_TEXTURE_FILTER_DEFAULT;
		}
	} else {
		texture_filter_cache = RSE::CanvasItemTextureFilter(texture_filter);
	}
}
```
As the TileMapLayer filter is set to inherit, it will check the parents upwards, but if no parent has an explicit value it will simply return TEXTURE_FILTER_PARENT_NODE, and this is the problem because the custom_overlay node responsible for drawing is inside the editors' viewport, not the scene root's where the default nearest has been set, so it will go upwards the editor ui tree and find a root with different values from the scene root's.

As the solution should we "hardcode" that node to have the same filter and repeat values as the TileMapLayer it is previewing? that seems to be the intended behavior from the code.

TLDR: The preview tile is correctly set to inherit, but it inherits from an editor's tree, not the scene's tree.
